      formula: "Concept: a ruler may reverse a policy when its costs clearly outweigh its benefits.",
      substitution: "Catholicism brought civil war and foreign enmity but no military help.",
      calculation: "With no firearms to suppress the rebellion, the policy only weakened his throne, so abandoning it was the rational choice.",
