  summary: "Placed on the defensive by Oromo expansion and Ottoman power, the Christian highland kingdom shifted its centre north to Lake Tana and tried to consolidate from Dembiya. The Jesuit mission, promising Portuguese firearms, led Susinyos to make Catholicism the state religion in 1622, but hasty imposition caused peasant and clergy rebellion and civil war. Fasiledes restored Orthodoxy and the Jesuits were expelled in 1632, after which the closed-door policy kept Europeans out until the early 19th century.",
