  summary: "Around 1636 Fasiledes made Gondar the permanent capital, and for about 150 years it was the political, economic and cultural centre of the Christian highland kingdom, famous for its castles, churches, art and scholarship. Its first three kings, especially Iyasu the Great, reformed law and trade, but after Iyasu was murdered in 1706 the monarchy weakened. The regency of Etege Mintiwab and the growing power of the regional lords prepared the way for the Zemene Mesafint in 1769.",
